==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sich}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sih}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sik}}. Compare {{cog|yi|זיך}}, {{cog|nl|zich}}.

This pronoun was originally restricted to the accusative case, while simple personal pronouns were used in the dative. Dative use of {{m|gmh||sich}} in {{m+|gmh|-}} was restricted to northern dialects of [[Central German]]. In Early Modern German, a dative {{m|de|sir}} also occurred, formed by analogy with {{m|de|mir}}, {{m|de|dir}}. An obstacle to the generalisation of this form was the use of {{m|de||sich}} in the plural, where there operated the conflicting analogy with the merged accusative/dative forms {{m|de|uns}}, {{m|de|euch}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/zɪç/}}
* {{audio|de|De-sich.ogg|audio}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|de|pronoun|both accusative and dative}}

